# Cross-origin isolation for expo-sqlite's WASM backend.
#
# The web build stores its database via wa-sqlite, which needs
# SharedArrayBuffer, which browsers only expose to a cross-origin isolated
# document. Without these two headers the page loads and then fails to open
# its database — no gear, no locations, no journeys — which looks nothing
# like a missing HTTP header.
#
# metro.config.js sets the same pair for the local dev server, but its own
# comment notes it "only runs inside the local Metro/Expo CLI process", so
# production hosting has to set them itself.
#
# COEP is `credentialless`, not `require-corp`: it still isolates the
# document, but doesn't require every cross-origin resource the app loads
# (CARTO map tiles, Google Places/Routes responses) to opt in with its own
# CORP header. See DECISIONS.md 2026-07-22.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
